# Notification copy

- Kinds, job names, and database IDs are not display copy. Give each push-capable
  kind readable event-specific copy; avoid generic fallbacks and payload fragments.
- `sourceLabel` is optional person/group/article context, never a raw kind or
  filler such as “From notifications.”
- Actor activity needs an action in its title and subtitle, such as “Checked in:”.
  iOS Communication notifications replace the title with the actor's name and may
  omit the subtitle, so `apnsBodyWithVisibleAction` also folds the action into the
  body. DMs retain message-style bodies; system kinds do not repeat their title
  as a subtitle. Preserve group context where applicable.
- Rows, websocket payloads, and pushes may differ in length but must describe the
  same event consistently. Keep previews appropriate for their audience.

Read `notification-push-copy.ts`, `notification-push.rules.ts`, and
`notification-push-delivery.service.ts` under `src/modules/notifications` before
changing copy. Extend the kind table and affected context assertions in
`notification-push.service.spec.ts`, including missing actor/group/preview cases.
